# video_life in the emulator's window (ECP5_GUI_SCRIPT; see gui/src/trace.rs).
# The Monitor window opens by itself when the design drives the GPDI pads.
# For the first 15 s nothing is pressed, so the frames the window decodes from
# the pads are those of the power-on start pattern, whose CRCs the design
# prints on the UART (and the board printed after a restart): gui_run.py
# compares them. Then the buttons, each held for a second: the design
# debounces them for 10 ms (250 000 clocks), which the window may take most
# of a second to run.
0 rate max
0 run
1 board 3d
15 button 1 down   # FIRE1: fill the world with random soup
16 button 1 up
23 button 2 down   # FIRE2: pause
24 button 2 up
27 button 6 down   # RIGHT: one generation while paused
28 button 6 up
31 button 2 down   # FIRE2: run again
32 button 2 up
35 button 3 down   # UP: faster (4 -> 2 frames per generation)
36 button 3 up
50 quit
